{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "c1111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
    "name": "Clinical Service — Patient Intake",
    "description": "End-to-end tests for the clinical-service Patient Intake Form API.\n\n**Run order**:\n1. `Setup / Login` — stores JWT in {{token}}\n2. `Happy Path / Submit form (valid)` — creates a form, stores id in {{formId}}\n3. Any `Validation failures` request — should return 400\n4. `Authenticated reads` — list + get by id\n5. `Admin / Update diagnosis and notes` — PATCHes the form\n\nRequires:\n- clinical-service running on http://localhost:8081\n- auth-service running on http://localhost:8080\n- Environment `Infra-X Local` selected in the top-right of Postman",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Setup",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (auth-service) — saves token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('has token', () => pm.expect(body.token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "pm.environment.set('token', body.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"admin\",\n  \"password\": \"admin\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{authUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{authUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Logs in as the seeded admin user in auth-service and stores the JWT into the `token` environment variable so subsequent requests can use it."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Happy Path",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Submit form (valid, full body) — saves formId",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('has id', () => pm.expect(body.id).to.be.a('number'));",
                  "pm.test('firstName is uppercase', () => pm.expect(body.firstName).to.equal('MAX'));",
                  "pm.test('symptoms include FEVER', () => pm.expect(body.symptoms).to.include('FEVER'));",
                  "pm.environment.set('formId', body.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"firstName\": \"MAX\",\n  \"lastName\": \"MUSTER\",\n  \"dateOfBirth\": \"1990-05-01\",\n  \"streetName\": \"HAUPTSTRASSE\",\n  \"streetNumber\": \"42\",\n  \"city\": \"BERLIN\",\n  \"postalCode\": \"10115\",\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"+49 30 1234567\",\n  \"emailAddress\": \"max@example.com\",\n  \"symptoms\": [\"FEVER\", \"COUGH\", \"HEADACHE\"],\n  \"otherSymptoms\": \"sore throat\",\n  \"allergies\": [\"POLLEN\", \"NUTS\"],\n  \"otherAllergies\": \"bee stings\",\n  \"medications\": [\"IBUPROFEN\"],\n  \"otherMedications\": null,\n  \"preExistingConditions\": [\"ASTHMA\"],\n  \"otherPreExistingConditions\": null\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{clinicalUrl}}/api/clinical/forms",
              "host": ["{{clinicalUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "clinical", "forms"]
            },
            "description": "Public endpoint. No Authorization header needed. Stores the returned id in {{formId}} for use in later requests."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Submit form (minimal — only required fields)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"firstName\": \"ANNA\",\n  \"lastName\": \"SCHMIDT\",\n  \"dateOfBirth\": \"1985-03-15\",\n  \"streetName\": \"BAHNHOFSTRASSE\",\n  \"streetNumber\": \"7\",\n  \"city\": \"MUENCHEN\",\n  \"postalCode\": \"80331\",\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"+49 89 55512345\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{clinicalUrl}}/api/clinical/forms",
              "host": ["{{clinicalUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "clinical", "forms"]
            },
            "description": "Only the required personal-info fields. email is optional, medical arrays are optional."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
